# Per-example lockfiles, created by running `npm install` inside an example folder. Only the
# shared framework-level lockfile is tracked. See the explanation in /examples/README.md.
#
# One pattern per framework name the install globs accept (`examples/package.json`'s
# `internal.framework_dirs` and `scripts/clean-subpackages.mjs`), in both categories, including
# names no directory uses today: `examples:version` copies a tree verbatim, and a name with no
# pattern puts its leaf lockfiles back within reach of the release job's bare `git add .`. A stale
# name silently ignores nothing, which is how `angular`, `react` and `vue` left 5 of the 23 leaf
# paths uncovered while the directories were named `angular-wrapper`, `react-wrapper` and `vue3`.
*/docs/angular/*/package-lock.json
*/docs/angular-wrapper/*/package-lock.json
*/docs/js/*/package-lock.json
*/docs/react/*/package-lock.json
*/docs/react-wrapper/*/package-lock.json
*/docs/ts/*/package-lock.json
*/docs/vue/*/package-lock.json
*/docs/vue3/*/package-lock.json
*/visual-tests/angular/*/package-lock.json
*/visual-tests/angular-wrapper/*/package-lock.json
*/visual-tests/js/*/package-lock.json
*/visual-tests/react/*/package-lock.json
*/visual-tests/react-wrapper/*/package-lock.json
*/visual-tests/ts/*/package-lock.json
*/visual-tests/vue/*/package-lock.json
*/visual-tests/vue3/*/package-lock.json
